A||||5||RossT||stock 15X7 gt rim on 88gt front||||1||
Z||000000||RossT||12-13-2000||02:02 AM||||I am thinking of having a second set of rims for my 88gt.  After viewing some of the before and after pics of refinished 86-87gt 15X7 rims, I thought I would like to do the same.  But some have said that using the 15X7 rim on the front of an 88gt make them stick out to far.  Wouldn't it look the same as the 86-87gt ? Or does the upgraded suspension on the 88gt make the 7 inch rim stick out to much?  <P>Anyone here have the stock 7" rim on an 88gt?<P>Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||JetroGT||12-13-2000||06:47 AM||||The 88GT suspension is designed to use the 15x6 in the front. I have seen the 15x7 in the front of 88's and it looks like any other year fast back. But by putting them on you may be taking away some handeling. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Tom88gt||12-13-2000||01:01 PM||||I bought my 88 with the wheels reversed but not the tires.  15x7 front and 15x6 rear.  I would have never noticed until another Fiero driver told me.  I raced SCCA with them backwards.  I lost but was inexperienced.  I later switched tires and wheels and did not notice any difference in driving or looks.  But I didn't measure (track width or lateral Gs) so I can't say for sure.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Black88GT||12-13-2000||03:20 PM||||As Raydar already mentioned, The spacing from hub to hub on the front of the 88s was increased.  I have seen '86-'87 GT wheels on an 88 coupe and it looked like crap.  Ask Mike L. (hyptnotise)....<P>When I got both of my '88s, they had the wheels reversed.  Probably people at the tire place thought it was FWD...<P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD||||reg||1
Z||000004||RossT||12-13-2000||04:36 PM||||Thanks guys, I think I will be looking for a set of the 6 inch rims for the front!!<P>Thats funny about the reversals.  My current rims are stamped "back only" and "front only"<BR>on the inside!!||||reg||1
Z||000005||Formula88||03-27-2001||11:09 PM||||When I got my Formula, the wheels were reversed, but not the tires, as well.  I noticed the car was very squirrely in corners and wanted to oversteer quite easily until I had the wheels swapped.  Also, the reason behind the different front wheels is that the steering rack on the 88 is 1" wider than the 87 and earlier cars.  That's why 87 wheels will stick out. ||||reg||1
